        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Unification of Italy</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">the Italian Peninsula and its outlying isles: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a>, the central duchies, the Papal States, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>; exiles worked from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and elsewhere abroad</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">revolts of the 1820s and 1830s; revolutions and the First War of Independence 1848–1849; Second War of Independence 1859; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Garibaldi</a>'s expedition 1860; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> proclaimed 1861; Third War of Independence 1866; capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> 1870; capital moved to Rome 1871</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Leading figures</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-mazzini">Giuseppe Mazzini</a>, founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/young-italy">Young Italy</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand">Expedition of the Thousand</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camillo-benso-count-of-cavour">Camillo Benso, Count of Cavour</a>, Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a>, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and then of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>; Charles Albert, King of Sardinia until 1849</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> as capital from 1871; Italian speakers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trentino">Trentino</a> and Venezia Giulia remained outside its borders until 1918–1920</span></div>
