    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> of 1814–15 restored the old patchwork of Italian governments, and risings against it in the 1820s and 1830s were put down with Austrian help.</li><li>After the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolutions-of-1848">revolutions of 1848</a>–1849 the patriots concluded that unification would need a strong monarchy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, the expulsion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> with French help, and not the pope as leader.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> was proclaimed on 17 March 1861 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> was captured on 20 September 1870, but the new state was built on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>'s institutions and left lasting regional grievances.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>From 1859 the slogan &quot;Viva VERDI&quot; spread through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> as an acronym for Viva Vittorio Emanuele Re D'Italia, a cry for King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

